  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match both the tenant and the owner and have `deleted_at IS NULL`. `python3 checks/public.py` passes, including the new checks.\n\n- **`src/repository.py`**:\n  - `find` and `listing` now take `tenant` and `owner` and filter on `tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`, with `id=?` added for `find`.\n  - `listing` keeps `ORDER BY id`.\n  - All values are bound parameters.\n  - Results are still dictionaries with only `id`, `title` and `body`, so no deletion metadata is returned.\n- **`src/service.py`**: both functions now pass `tenant` and `owner` through to the repository. Before, `tenant` was ignored, `get_document` ignored `owner` as well, and neither excluded deleted rows.\n- **`checks/public.py`**: I appended checks to the existing file rather than creating a new one. They cover:\n  - `get_document` returns `None` for other-owner, other-tenant, deleted and missing IDs.\n  - `list_documents` leaves out those rows and returns the rest ordered by id.\n  - Tenant and owner names containing quotes work, and a quote-based injection string matches nothing.\n\nI also ran a `sed` over `checks/public.py` to delete a leftover, unused `rows = [...]` block from my first draft. It only touched that block, and the check file runs cleanly.",
